  "notes": "A casual suru-verb made from the everyday noun お{茶|ちゃ} (tea). The お is fixed here — {茶|ちゃ}する is not used.\n\nUSAGE:\nMost often heard as an invitation: お{茶|ちゃ}しない?, お{茶|ちゃ}しよう. It is too casual for business settings, where {打|う}ち{合|あ}わせ or お{茶|ちゃ}でも{飲|の}みませんか would be used instead. Common among friends and especially among younger speakers.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- お{茶|ちゃ}しない?: want to get tea?\n- お{茶|ちゃ}でもする: to have tea or something\n- カフェでお{茶|ちゃ}する: to hang out at a café\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- お{茶|ちゃ}を{飲|の}む: to drink tea — literal, about the drink rather than the outing\n- {一服|いっぷく}する: to take a break — a short rest, often alone",
